# The backup schedule, run by supercronic inside the backup container. Times are UTC (Lagos is UTC+1);
# the heavy jobs sit in the quiet hours and share one lock, so they never overlap. Each job records its
# result in the backup_runs table, which the admin console's System Health page reads.
#
# Seven fields (with seconds) for the WAL shipper: every 20 seconds.
*/20 * * * * * *  nf-backup-run wal-push
# Logical dump of the whole database (portable to any PostgreSQL 16+), every 6 hours.
17 */6 * * *      nf-backup-run dump
# Physical base backup for point-in-time recovery, daily.
37 2 * * *        nf-backup-run base
# Profile photos, the JWT key, the Caddyfile and the settings list, daily.
47 3 * * *        nf-backup-run files
# Retention and the repository integrity check, daily.
7 4 * * *         nf-backup-run maintain
# Optional second copy at another provider (BACKUP_MIRROR), daily.
27 5 * * *        nf-backup-run mirror
# The restore drill's result, from the bucket into the console, within ten minutes of the run (one small
# read each time; a result is recorded once).
*/10 * * * *      nf-backup-run drill-status
